 ## Overview
-`VoxelizationGrid` is a data structure representing an explicit voxelization grid, defining spatial bounds, grid dimensions, and voxel sizes in 3D space [S2, S3, unofficial]. It serves as a base class for managing a 3D voxel grid in world space, providing utilities for coordinate conversion, ray intersection, and mesh generation [S3, unofficial]. It focuses on foundational storage and indexing logic rather than the rendering pipeline itself [G].
