 ## Operating characteristics
-*   **Time Complexity:** Coordinate conversion is O(1). Ray marching is O(N) where N is the number of voxels intersected. Mesh generation for all cells is O(N).
+*   **Time Complexity:** Coordinate conversion is O(1) [G]. Ray marching is O(N) where N is the number of voxels intersected. Mesh generation for all cells is O(N).
 *   **Memory Complexity:** O(N) where N is the total number of voxels (`xCount * yCount * zCount`). The C++ implementation stores pointers to `Voxel` structs, adding overhead [S1, unofficial].
 *   **Memory Scaling:** Memory usage scales cubically. A 1024^3 grid requires 1 GB, which is too much for most cases [S4, unofficial]. Solutions include chunking (e.g., 16x16x256 blocks) and sparse storage (octree) [S4, unofficial].
